  "body": "## Change and scope\n\nAt base `0fdd7d82de03e43c9e5a1000dfbcd380d1b687d2`, `scripts/experiments/complex_centers.py:verify_factor` still used the historical nested entrywise loop over all scatter/gather pairs. Ross Richardson\u2019s opt-in adapter `research/central-factor-packed/` already proved an injective packed-row algorithm with identical receipts. This PR wires that equivalent check into the **production** source used by `scripts/audit_complex_centers.py` / `make verify-certificates`.\n\nOnly the source pin for `scripts/experiments/complex_centers.py` changes inside `certificates/dyadic-central-factor.json`. Every coefficient is still checked; factor generators, side/phase obligations and the retained historical `2^-31` language are unchanged.\n\n**Tooling improvement; no new kappa.** Selected frontier untouched.\n\n## Result\n\nOn Linux / CPython 3.12.3 (Linux-6.12.94+-x86_64-with-glibc2.39), five alternating fresh-process pairs gave median wall time:\n\n- **factor-only:** **2.615 \u2192 0.059 seconds (44.06\u00d7)**\n- **complete audit:** **5.784 \u2192 3.356 seconds (1.72\u00d7)**\n\nTiming is host-descriptive and is not a correctness gate. Every `verify_factor` receipt matches the baseline checker fieldwise.\n\nPackage: `research/central-factor-production/`.\n\n## Validation\n\n```sh\npython3.12 -I -B research/central-factor-production/verify.py\npython3.12 -I -O -B research/central-factor-production/verify.py\npython3.12 -B scripts/research_package.py --package research/central-factor-production\npython3.12 -I -B research/central-factor-production/benchmark.py --rounds 5\n```\n\nExpected:\n\n```text\nPASS_CENTRAL_FACTOR_PRODUCTION heights=[8, 10, 12, 18, 26] ... no_new_kappa\nPASS_REGISTERED_RESEARCH_PACKAGE research/central-factor-production outcome=completed\nPASS_IDENTICAL_CENTRAL_FACTOR_PRODUCTION_RECEIPTS\n```\n\nDefault verify is read-only. Coefficient-mismatch and temp-copy corruption controls reject; `require` gates remain under `-O`. Full `make verify`, selected cold replay, Lean, and multiplication-theorem obligations were not rerun for this isolated historical-checker change.\n\n## Overlap and credit\n\nClosest priors (different delivery): Ross Richardson\u2019s `research/central-factor-packed/` (opt-in packed adapter; this is the production wiring), [CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds#756](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/756), [CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds#2117](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/2117) (same `dyadic-central-factor.json`, different pin key `disjoint_tensor.py`). No competing open PR on production `verify_factor` at refresh.\n\nDouglas R. Colkitt authored the dyadic central factor and original checker. Ross Richardson authored the packed algorithm. Prepared by Wentao Li ([VictorLiwentao](https://github.com/VictorLiwentao), [@Is__Victor](https://x.com/Is__Victor)) with substantial AI assistance, under Apache-2.0.",
